<title>UK: IEA supply/demand highlights - end March report.</title>
<headline>IEA supply/demand highlights - end March report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table highlights the oil supply-demand and stock estimates included in the International Energy Agency's latest Monthly Oil Market Report.</p>
<p>Figures in million barrels per day.</p>
<p>		  1994 1995 1Q96 2Q96 3Q96 4Q96 1996 1Q97 2Q97 3Q97 4Q97 1997</p>
<p>DEMAND</p>
<p> OECD	   40.0 40.4 42.1 39.6 40.7 42.2 41.1 42.2 40.3 41.3 43.0 41.7</p>
<p> NON-OECD     28.9 29.9 31.0 30.3 30.3 31.5 30.7 31.9 31.5 31.4 33.1 32.0</p>
<p> TOTAL	  68.9 70.2 73.1 69.9 71.0 73.6 71.9 74.2 71.8 72.6 76.1 73.7</p>
<p>SUPPLY</p>
<p> NON-OPEC     41.6 42.4 43.3 43.2 43.4 44.3 43.6 44.6 44.6 45.3 47.2 45.4</p>
<p> OPEC CRUDE   24.7 25.1 25.7 25.6 25.9 26.2 25.9 27.0</p>
<p> OPEC NGLS     2.4  2.4  2.5  2.6  2.7  2.7  2.6  2.8  2.9  3.0 3.1 3.0</p>
<p> TOTAL OPEC   27.0 27.5 28.2 28.2 28.6 29.0 28.5 29.9</p>
<p>TOTAL SUPPLY  68.6 69.9 71.5 71.4 72.0 73.2 72.0 74.4</p>
<p> OPEC CALL*   24.9 25.4 27.4 24.0 24.9 26.7 25.7 26.8 24.2 24.4 25.8 25.3</p>
<p> IND STOCKS   +0.1 -0.3 -1.5 +1.2 +0.5 -0.5 -0.1 -0.1</p>
<p>TOT STCK BAL  -0.2 -0.4 -1.6  1.6 +1.0 -0.5 +0.1 +0.3</p>
<p> FSU NET EXP   2.4  2.4  2.4  2.8  2.8  2.9  2.7  2.8  2.9  2.9 2.7 2.8</p>
<p>* Implied call on OPEC crude equals total demand minus total non-OPEC supply minus OPEC NGLs. Thus includes &quot;miscellaneous to balance&quot; for historical time periods.</p>
